[{"text": "The assembly will hear an address by his", "start": 1.04, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "excellency", "start": 4.56, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "vier, prime minister of the republic of", "start": 6.72, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "Guinabiso.", "start": 9.519, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "I request protocol to to escort his", "start": 11.04, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "excellency", "start": 14.639, "duration": 7.64}, {"text": "and invite him to address the assembly.", "start": 16.64, "duration": 5.639}, {"text": "President,", "start": 33.76, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": ">> Mr. President,", "start": 35.2, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "distinguished heads of state and", "start": 37.6, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "government, Mr. Secretary General,", "start": 39.28, "duration": 5.88}, {"text": "ladies and gentlemen,", "start": 41.52, "duration": 3.64}, {"text": "I have the honor of addressing this", "start": 46.16, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "august assembly on behalf of the", "start": 48.719, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "government and the people of the", "start": 51.44, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Republic of Guinea Bisau. Allow me to", "start": 53.92, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "congratulate Mr. Khalil Raman on his", "start": 56.8, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "election as president of the General", "start": 60.0, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "Assembly of the United Nations. I am", "start": 62.079, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "confident that his governmental and", "start": 64.96, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "diplomatic experience will help guide", "start": 67.6, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "the work of this assembly", "start": 70.08, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "with balance and in a spirit of", "start": 72.64, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "dialogue.", "start": 75.119, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "I also commend Miss Analena Barbok", "start": 76.64, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "for the dedication she demonstrated", "start": 81.439, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "during her term of office and for her", "start": 83.6, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "efforts to strengthen multilateralism", "start": 86.4, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "and international cooperation. It is a", "start": 89.6, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "particular pleasure for me to express", "start": 92.32, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "our appreciation to the Secretary", "start": 94.24, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "General of the United Nations, Mr.", "start": 96.159, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "Antonio Gutish, for his tireless", "start": 99.119, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "commitment to the defense of peace and", "start": 102.24, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "to the search for solutions to the many", "start": 106.159, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "challenges facing humanity.", "start": 108.32, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "Ladies and gentlemen, yesterday,", "start": 111.119, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "September 24th, the people of Guineabis", "start": 113.759, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "South celebrated the 53rd anniversary of", "start": 116.32, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "our national independence.", "start": 119.92, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "This date of profound significance for", "start": 122.399, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "our people, invites us to reflect on the", "start": 125.2, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "value of freedom, sovereignty, and the", "start": 128.399, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "dignity of peoples. It is in this spirit", "start": 130.959, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "that I bring to this assembly a message", "start": 134.48, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "of peace, freedom, and fraternity to all", "start": 137.44, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "the nations of the world.", "start": 140.959, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "In the firm hope that every people may", "start": 143.599, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "live in peace, fully exercise its", "start": 146.48, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "rights, and freely chart its own path", "start": 148.64, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "towards development and prosperity. We", "start": 151.92, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "live in an interdependent world marked", "start": 155.36, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "by growing uncertainty and by challenges", "start": 158.239, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "that transcend borders. Climate change,", "start": 161.599, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "transnational organized crime,", "start": 164.239, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "terrorism, structural inequalities, the", "start": 166.56, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "burden of debt, and insufficient", "start": 169.76, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "financing for development continue to", "start": 172.8, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "undermine our efforts towards", "start": 176.0, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "sustainable development.", "start": 177.68, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "Devastating conflicts also persist in", "start": 180.4, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "several regions of the world as do", "start": 183.12, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "security challenges particularly in the", "start": 185.44, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "Sahel.", "start": 188.0, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "In this context, Guineabis considers it", "start": 189.599, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "essential to strengthen the", "start": 192.879, "duration": 3.601}, {"text": "international community support to the", "start": 194.319, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "most affected countries in the region.", "start": 196.48, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Ladies and gentlemen, the United Nations", "start": 199.36, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "remains an essential pillar of", "start": 202.0, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "multilateralism", "start": 204.319, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "and a privileged forum for dialogue,", "start": 206.0, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "cooperation, and the search for", "start": 208.959, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "collective solutions to the challenges", "start": 210.72, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "facing humanity.", "start": 212.879, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "It must be acknowledged, however, that", "start": 215.44, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "in certain circumstances,", "start": 217.76, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "the expectations that peoples have", "start": 219.92, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "placed in it have not always been met", "start": 222.72, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "with a response commensurate with their", "start": 225.2, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "aspirations.", "start": 228.959, "duration": 3.761}, {"text": "This reality should not lead us to", "start": 230.799, "duration": 3.921}, {"text": "question the foundations of the", "start": 232.72, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "multilateral system but rather to", "start": 234.72, "duration": 4.719}, {"text": "strengthen the effectiveness,", "start": 237.28, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "representativeness and capacity for", "start": 239.439, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "action of international institutions. It", "start": 241.68, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "is in incumbent upon member states to", "start": 245.2, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "renew their commitment to", "start": 247.599, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "multilateralism that is more effective,", "start": 249.92, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "more inclusive and more responsive to", "start": 252.4, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "the aspirations of peoples. We also", "start": 255.36, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "consider it urgent", "start": 257.28, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "to reform the architecture of global", "start": 260.0, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "government so that it reflects the", "start": 262.079, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "geopolitical realities of the 21st", "start": 263.919, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "century. It is essential that Africa", "start": 267.04, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "have more adequate and effective", "start": 269.28, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "representation in the international", "start": 270.96, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "institutions that play a s central role", "start": 272.72, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "in shaping responses to the challenges", "start": 275.759, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "of peace, security and development. The", "start": 278.56, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "reform of United Nations Security", "start": 281.04, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Council must reflect the legitimate", "start": 282.96, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "aspirations of the African continent and", "start": 286.24, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "ensure fairer, permanent, and effective", "start": 288.479, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "representation in keeping with the", "start": 291.199, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "principle of a more inclusive,", "start": 293.6, "duration": 3.92}, {"text": "equitable, and representative", "start": 295.44, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "international order. Guineabis welcomes", "start": 297.52, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "the efforts of the United Nations to", "start": 300.72, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "achieve achieve a lasting political", "start": 302.88, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "solution to the question of Western", "start": 305.52, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "Sahara. We welcome the adoption of", "start": 308.0, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Security Council resolution 2797", "start": 310.32, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "of 2025 and view favorably the autonomy", "start": 313.36, "duration": 6.559}, {"text": "initiative presented by the Kingdom of", "start": 317.36, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "Morocco as a basis for resolving this", "start": 319.919, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "dispute. Ladies and gentlemen, on", "start": 323.12, "duration": 6.639}, {"text": "November 26, 2025 during the electoral", "start": 325.84, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "process, the constitutional order in", "start": 329.759, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "Gene Bisau was interrupted and", "start": 332.8, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "transitional bodies were established.", "start": 335.199, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "A one-year transition period was set", "start": 338.8, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "with the aim of creating the conditions", "start": 341.68, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "necessary for the restoration of", "start": 343.919, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "constitutional order. Within this", "start": 346.4, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "framework, the constitutional review", "start": 349.12, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "process has been completed and the new", "start": 351.36, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "constitution of the republic was", "start": 354.4, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "approved by popular referendum on August", "start": 356.32, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "30th, 2026.", "start": 359.68, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "This process is an important milestone", "start": 363.12, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "in the transition and in the restoration", "start": 365.28, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "of constitutional order in the country.", "start": 367.919, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "The government is committed to creating", "start": 370.639, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "the conditions necessary for the", "start": 372.479, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "presidential and legislative elections", "start": 374.479, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "scheduled for December 6 of this year to", "start": 377.52, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "be held in an inclusive, free,", "start": 381.199, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "transparent, and credible manner. I take", "start": 383.6, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "this opportunity to express our", "start": 387.039, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "gratitude to the economic community of", "start": 389.039, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "West African States, Echoas, the African", "start": 391.84, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "Union, the United Nations and our other", "start": 395.12, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "instit international partners for their", "start": 398.8, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "engagement and support in the efforts to", "start": 401.6, "duration": 7.039}, {"text": "ensure a return to constitutional mon", "start": 405.039, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "normaly in our country.", "start": 408.639, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "Ladies and gentlemen, three decades ago,", "start": 411.44, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "Gilbisaw had the honor of serving as a", "start": 413.68, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "non-permanent member of the United", "start": 416.24, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "Nations Security Council. Today, as we", "start": 418.24, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "reaffirm our commitment to the purposes", "start": 421.759, "duration": 4.241}, {"text": "and principles of the charter of the", "start": 423.84, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "United Nations and to the promotion of", "start": 426.0, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "international peace and security, I wish", "start": 428.479, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "to reiterate that Guineabis is a", "start": 431.44, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "candidate for non-permanent membership", "start": 434.319, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "of the security council for the term", "start": 437.12, "duration": 7.199}, {"text": "2028 2029. Our vision of the world rests", "start": 439.599, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "fundamentally on four key words.", "start": 444.319, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "Prevention, dialogue, cooperation,", "start": 447.039, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "peace. We will work with all member", "start": 449.84, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "states to advance essential", "start": 452.479, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "consensusbased priorities for Guinea", "start": 454.8, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "Bisau. As a developing country,", "start": 458.0, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "multilateralism and respect for", "start": 460.479, "duration": 6.801}, {"text": "international law are not mere concepts.", "start": 462.88, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "They are an existential necessity.", "start": 467.28, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "Ladies and gentlemen, Guinea Bisau", "start": 469.599, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "follows with concern the humanitarian", "start": 472.0, "duration": 4.639}, {"text": "consequences of the measures imposed", "start": 474.56, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "against Cuba. We therefore reiterate our", "start": 476.639, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "call for the lifting of the economic,", "start": 479.919, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "commercial, and financial embargo as", "start": 482.0, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "well as other restrictive measures that", "start": 484.96, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "affect the Cuban people in essential", "start": 487.52, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "sectors of that country's economy. Over", "start": 490.08, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "the past decades, this assembly has", "start": 493.52, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "built consensus and undertaken numerous", "start": 495.759, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "commitments towards the achievement of", "start": 499.28, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "common goals.", "start": 502.319, "duration": 3.761}, {"text": "Many of these commitments, however,", "start": 504.319, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "remain unfulfilled. Enormous gaps", "start": 506.08, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "persist in financing for development and", "start": 509.199, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "climate action alongside high levels of", "start": 511.84, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "poverty and social inequality and a", "start": 515.12, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "growing and unsustainable debt burden on", "start": 518.24, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "the economies of developing countries.", "start": 521.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "In the face of this reality, we need", "start": 523.919, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "more multilateralism,", "start": 526.16, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "effective international cooperation, and", "start": 528.56, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "more united and determined collective", "start": 531.04, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "action. No country, however powerful,", "start": 533.92, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "can face today's challenges alone. It is", "start": 536.959, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "in this spirit of cooperation,", "start": 539.92, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "solidarity, and peace that Guineabis", "start": 542.0, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "will continue to work with all member", "start": 545.04, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "states to uphold the principles", "start": 546.88, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "enshrined in the charter of the United", "start": 549.279, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "Nations and to build a better future, a", "start": 551.6, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "future of peace, development, and", "start": 554.72, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "well-being for present and future", "start": 556.64, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "generations.", "start": 559.2, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "Guinea Bisau uh thanks you and God bless", "start": 560.959, "duration": 7.121}, {"text": "all. Thank you.", "start": 564.88, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": ">> On behalf of the assembly, I wish to", "start": 568.08, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "thank the prime minister of the Republic", "start": 570.56, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "of Guinabis.", "start": 572.08, "duration": 3.16}]